<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandela dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th–13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chandela dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from the ninth to the thirteenth century, first as feudatories of the Gurjara-Pratiharas and from the tenth century independently. Their capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a>, where they built the famous temple complex, and they held the great fortresses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinjar-fort">Kalanjara</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ajaigarh">Ajaygarh</a>. Weakened by Chahamana and Ghurid attacks, they lost Kalanjara to Qutb al-Din Aibak in 1203.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty.jpg" alt="Chandela dynasty" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chandelas_of_Jejakabhukti._Sallakshana_Varman._Circa_1120-1135_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
